{
  "_about": "Ranking baseline expectations for the five sample ToRs. `requirements` are the exact grid rows a sensible hiring manager would set (app Requirement shape; levels: slight = Nice to have, strong = Important, must = Required; expertise rows name items of the unified list, profiles-membership §6; language rows carry `min`: working = Working or above, fluent = Fluent only). `expected_top` should land in the top 10 (ideally top 5). `expected_extraction` is what a good extractor should suggest from the JD. `checks` are deliberate test cases; `tier_order` and `fluent_only` score in-memory variants of one profile (Core / Strong / Working on one item; the Required language at Working). `ablate` lists rows to drop as a what-if (the report shows the top 10 with and without them). Read by scripts/ranking-baseline.ts.",
